-WLED_GLOBAL bool       doInitBusses  _INIT(false);
+// volatile: written by the AsyncTCP web-server task (handleSettingsSet) and read by loop(),
+// which run as different tasks and typically on different cores. Without volatile the compiler
+// may cache this read in a register or hoist it out of loop(), so the flag set by a settings
+// POST is never observed - finalizeInit() never runs, busConfigs is never cleared (it grows
+// without bound across saves) and the edited bus list is silently discarded, leaving the old
+// config to be written back. Latent for years; it becomes reproducible on the IDF5 platform
+// where the toolchain jumps from GCC 8.4 to GCC 15.2 and optimizes far more aggressively.
+WLED_GLOBAL volatile bool doInitBusses  _INIT(false);
